# Jira status

Keep status honest. Prefer a connected Jira / Atlassian MCP when ready
(`jira_get_transitions` → `jira_transition_issue`, backlog ↔ board moves when
the board id is known). Never invent a board id.

## Lifecycle

| Moment | Where | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Created with no start directive | Backlog | leave as created / backlog |
| User loads items “on deck” | Board | `To Do` (or host equivalent) |
| User pulls / starts a backlog item | Board first, then work | on-deck, then `In Progress` — never In Progress from backlog alone |
| Work starts on an item already on the board | Board | `In Progress` |
| Story/Bug: required delivery gates met (e.g. required PRs merged) | Board | `Done` |
| Task / Sub-task: deliverable complete (PR only if host requires) | Board | `Done` |
| Epic: goals met / children closed or cut | Board | `Done` |

## Moves

1. **On deck** — backlog → board when the user asks and a board id is known.
2. **Start** — never jump to `In Progress` from backlog alone. On-deck first
   when board moves apply, then `In Progress` when implementation begins.
3. **Done** — only after the type’s done bar is met. An open PR alone is not
   Done; stay `In Progress` until required merges (or Task deliverable) land.
4. If a transition fails, report the blocker — do not fake status in chat.

## Blockers

When an issue has an open inbound **is blocked by** link:

- Treat it as a hard gate until that blocker is `Done`.
- Say the blocker key(s) and refuse to start work on the blocked issue.
- Creating train links: earlier issue blocks later issue — do not reverse the
  arguments.

## Scope

- Do not invent a ticket so this status rule can run.
- Do not mark Done because chat “feels finished.”
